WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.602
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actress

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:07.139
and producer you know from
such shows as "8 Simple Rules"

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.374
and "The Big Bang Theory."

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:11.177
She's both starring in
and executive producing

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.579
the second season
of "The Flight Attendant,"

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.180
which returns to HBO Max
tomorrow.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.181
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.616
-Well, well, well.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:19.018
Hello, gorgeous.
-Hello, beauty.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.153
-You know, I have been seeing
you a lot at LAX lately.

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:22.522
Are you stalking me?

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.190
-I took a transpacific route.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.292
I am seeing all of the sights.
I'm eating all of the fish.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.526
-Mm-hmm.
-Yeah.

00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:29.195
-And doing the secret work
that's a secret job

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.663
that we can't talk about
because I'm doing it, too,

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:33.232
'cause it's so much fun!
-If I knew what you were

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:35.068
talking about, I would tell you
that what you do and what I do

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.869
are two very different things.
-Right.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:37.971
-And we're not
gonna talk about it.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.872
-...talk about it.

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:42.875
-Please welcome back to the show
Kaley Cuoco, everybody!

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:44.877
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:54.887 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:57.757 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:00.927
-I'm so happy to have you
back here in the studio!

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.728
-Hi, Seth!
Oh, it's so nice to be

00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:04.564
in person and see you.
-Isn't it great to be in person?

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:05.898
-Yes.
-We've done in-person before.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:07.700
We've done Zoom.
And this is -- let's be honest,

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.368
this is the better of the two.
-This is so much better.

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:10.469
I can high-five you.
-There you go.

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:11.470
-We can touch.
-There you go.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.705
-Yes, I like it.
I like it.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.908
-And do not take this
the wrong way.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.242
I just --
-Okay, yeah, me too.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.411
-You can't be too safe
with new variants.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.645
-You're right.
-You travel a lot.

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:21.747
There we go.
-You're so right about that.

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:24.650
-Hey, so I want to talk --
The last time we talked --

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.552
You have a rescue dog.
-Yes.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.554
-With a great name
for a rescue dog.

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.957
I feel like if I say it,
it might even come off as mean,

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:32.492
so why don't you say it?
-Dump Truck?

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.992
-Dump Truck.
-Yeah, Dump Truck, yeah.

00:01:33.992 --> 00:01:35.194
Dumpy.
-Dumpy?

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:36.962
-Yeah, known as --
he answers to Dumpy.

00:01:36.962 --> 00:01:38.598
-He answers to Dumpy.
-Obviously.

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.133
-And did you --
was this something,

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:43.169
the minute you saw Dumpy, you
knew that this was the name?

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.737
-You know,
he came with that name.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.406
I don't think you can take
that name away from someone.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.007
-No, you can't, yeah.
-No.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.809
-You can't be like, "Sebastian!"
-No.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:50.843
-Yeah.
-No.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.846
He is a Dump Truck, all the way.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.580
-And he really answers to Dumpy.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.981
-Although, he's a little guy.
-He's a little guy.

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:57.283
-I think when you hear
Dump Truck,

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.385
you might think a bigger dog.
-Very small and old.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.420
-Now, I should note --
Well, hold on, 'cause this is --

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.888
I want to
note that there's a reason Dumpy

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:05.958
in this photo is getting makeup.
-So, Dumpy is --

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:07.326
-Dumpy doesn't always
get makeup.

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:10.563
-No, Dumpy got to do a scene
in "The Flight Attendant."

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:13.800
-Okay. Gotcha.
-And he got a very big head

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.535
and brought his glam squad
for this scene.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.269
-Yeah.
-If you look closely

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:19.271
in the first episode,
you will spot him.

00:02:19.271 --> 00:02:22.542
So there is his --
-I do feel like that this is --

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.077
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.645
This is only the kind of
treatment a dog

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.680
who is like -- belongs to
the executive producer

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:28.848
and star of the show gets.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.417
-Yes, that's my chair
right there, Dumps.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.785
Yeah.
-Okay.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:36.355
Now, did -- did Dumpy
have to audition, or is this --

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:38.323
Did you pull strings?
-So here's what was interesting.

00:02:38.323 --> 00:02:39.592
We were looking for a dog

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.694
for this opening sequence
in the episode.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.395
We were thinking, like,
a big dog, a small dog.

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:45.698
I'm like, "Guys, we should
just offer this to Dumpy."

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.732
-Right.
-Full offer.

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:48.100
-Gotcha.
-He did not have to audition.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.468
-Got it.
-But he did --

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:51.237
You know, he wanted
his whole team to come.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.638
He wanted a trailer.
-Be honest.

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:55.074
Was -- because I would
be very nervous if I --

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.410
Like, I, for real, had my dog
come on this show once,

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.711
and it was --
-Did it make you nervous?

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.613
-Yeah, and she was a huge dud.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.147
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.147 --> 00:03:04.150
But it was my fault.
Like, she scares easily.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.085
She did not like being out here.
It was a huge mistake.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.287
-It was just a bad idea.
-But how did Dumpy do?

00:03:08.287 --> 00:03:11.023
-I was like a stage mom.

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:12.358
So he -- I wasn't actually

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:13.760
in the scene with him
at the beginning.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.595
I was off camera like,
"Look over here!"

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.230
I was crazy.
I was like one of those

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.031
stage moms people talk about.
-Yeah.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:20.566
-But he really performed.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:23.235
-He actually yawned on cue.
We got it on camera.

00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:24.603
-That's shocking.
-It was incredible.

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.172
-Yeah.
-It was like he prepped

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.974
his whole life.
All he does is yawn.

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:29.142
So it was perfect.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:31.043
-Well, he also is famously bored
by your work.

00:03:31.043 --> 00:03:35.147
-Famously bored,
like everybody else.

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:36.949
-But this is --
Let me just say --

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:38.484
That is not true,
but let me just say,

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.986
this, again,
is some strings pulled.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.822
You got -- now people should
know, in credits,

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.757
in closing credits of a show...
-Yes.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.960
-...it's a big deal to not have
to share the credit page.

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.962
-Yes. So -- yes,
exactly what he's saying.

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:52.798
So you get a single card.
That means you are really --

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:54.567
It takes a lot of negotiating.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.336
Teams negotiate that for their
actors to get a single card,

00:03:57.336 --> 00:03:59.505
their only name on the card
in the credits.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:03.809
So, Dumpy, since he is related
to the executive producer --

00:04:03.809 --> 00:04:05.077
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:08.381
-This is what you will see
in the first episode.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:09.983
-And I mean,
it's also very hard.

00:04:09.983 --> 00:04:11.483
Your agent
really has to negotiate...

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:13.152
-Two lines.
-...to get your a.k.a.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.121
in there, as well.
-Yeah! Exactly!

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.990
There were a lot of
unhappy guest actors.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.125
But Dumpy was very pleased
with this.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:21.994
-Hey, this show just took off
like a rocket ship

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:23.829
when it came out, now, I guess,
two years ago, right?

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:26.198
-Yes.
-And it got nominated

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:28.134
for a ton of awards.
I think people were so thrilled

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:29.468
to see you
doing something differently

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:31.503
after they had learned
to love you in another thing.

00:04:31.503 --> 00:04:34.473
-Thank you.
-But do you get a little nervous

00:04:34.473 --> 00:04:37.109
when you do a second season
of a show that was so embraced?

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:39.778
-Oh, my God, I did not
want to do a second season.

00:04:39.778 --> 00:04:41.080
I'm like,
"Guys, we got away with it."

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.514
-Right.
-"Let's go.

00:04:42.514 --> 00:04:44.350
Let's just walk out of here,
leave it.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.785
It was really good."

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:47.486
I was so shocked
that it did so well.

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:48.988
I hate to say that,
but I was so nervous

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:51.123
about doing something so new.
-Yeah.

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:52.324
-And then it did really well,

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:53.559
and I kind of thought
we should leave it alone.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:56.028
But then they came up
with some great ideas

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:57.729
and more international travel.

00:04:57.729 --> 00:04:59.899
We went to Iceland and Berlin,
and I had to dive in.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:02.935
And then they wrote me --
I played five Cassies this year.

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:04.269
-Which is -- I mean --
-Insane.

00:05:04.269 --> 00:05:06.472
-As an actor, it's both
thrilling, I would imagine,

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.140
to play five different
characters,

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:11.177
versions of yourself, but also,
I mean, it must be --

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.112
it just must feel
so burdensome at times.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:14.914
-Well, do you know who I don't
want to work with anymore?

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.082
-Who's that?
-Me.

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.483
-Yeah, I would imagine.
-It's a lot of me.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.785
That was a lot of me,
all day long.

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:21.020
-Right.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.254
-And now I know
how everyone else feels.

00:05:22.254 --> 00:05:23.722
-Well, there you go.
That's some empathy now.

00:05:23.722 --> 00:05:25.925
-It was a lot of empathy.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.326
-I worked with
a lot of tennis balls,

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:28.828
but it was just a lot of myself

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.563
and it was a very wild
experience, actually.

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.365
Very similar to "Orphan Black."
-Yeah.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.700
-We actually
talked to their team

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.301
and learned a lot
from how they did it.

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.336
It was a crazy, crazy time.
Crazy.

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:40.072
-That's great. You mentioned
you went to Berlin and Iceland.

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:41.473
Iceland is one of
the most beautiful countries

00:05:41.473 --> 00:05:43.142
I've ever been to.
When did you go?

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:45.010
-Over Christmas.
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.813
-Which I thought was insane.
-Yes.

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:48.313
-I'm like, "You guys, we're
gonna shoot there in December.

00:05:48.313 --> 00:05:49.949
It's like 20 degrees."

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.550
It ended up being incredible.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.619
-Also, that time of year,
I went for New Year's once.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:56.521
It was amazing, but it's like
bright for like 90 minutes.

00:05:56.521 --> 00:05:58.056
-Literally three hours.
-Yeah.

00:05:58.056 --> 00:05:59.492
-We have three hours of
sunshine.

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.094
-The sun doesn't go, like --

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:02.394
I feel like
the sun goes like this.

00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:03.696
-Yes.
-It, like, goes like...

00:06:03.696 --> 00:06:04.830
-Yeah.
-Just like --

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:06.499
-There's nothing.
-It just, like, comes out.

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:08.400
It's like, "Hi, bye!"
-"Hi, bye!

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.434
We're done now!"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:10.569
And you're like,
"Wait a minute!"

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:12.604
And then -- yeah, exactly.
It was crazy.

00:06:12.604 --> 00:06:13.773
But what I loved about it,

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.574
I'm kind of an elf
during the holidays.

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:17.476
-And it's like Christmas
just threw up.

00:06:17.476 --> 00:06:19.245
-Yeah.
-It's like you're at

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:21.080
the North Pole.
Everyone's singing,

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:24.450
there's Santas in the street,
Christmas music playing.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.486
-There's a lot of, like,
blood relations to Santa

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:28.054
that live there, I think.
-You're probably --

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.455
-Yeah, a lot of people
that know him.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.891
-That is right.
-Is it -- it's trolls or elves.

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:33.759
I feel like Iceland --
I get this wrong.

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:35.194
-Trolls!
-Yeah, they have --

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.262
-They're big on trolls there.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:37.463
-Yeah, they're, like,
big on trolls.

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:39.565
And not like, "ha ha" --
it's like, "No, this is

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:40.733
where trolls live," yeah.
-Real trolls.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.067
Yeah, it's really bizarre,
actually.

00:06:42.067 --> 00:06:43.168
-It's really bizarre.
-They have a lot of billboards

00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:44.603
of trolls.
-Uh-huh.

00:06:44.603 --> 00:06:45.704
-I didn't
really understand that.

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:46.973
-No.
-It was bizarre.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:49.642
-It's weird that they think
that would be, like,

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:51.577
magnetic to people.
-I don't understand that.

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:52.844
-Yeah, like, "I wanna go
where the trolls are."

00:06:52.844 --> 00:06:54.179
-Where the trolls are.

00:06:54.179 --> 00:06:55.547
-It's one of the most beautiful
places in the world.

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:56.949
-I -- I loved it.
-You know what?

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.250
I'm not gonna tell them how
to run their tourism board.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.285
They're obviously doing
very well.

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:00.819
-I know!
They are doing amazing.

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:02.221
And there's no COVID there,
by the way.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.389
-There you go.
-You're just in, like,

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:04.956
this little bubble.
-That's great.

00:07:04.956 --> 00:07:07.560
-I know.
-On set --

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.262
Now, historically,
are you a prank person on set?

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:11.764
-Okay. I love pranks.

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.098
-Okay.
I do not.

00:07:13.098 --> 00:07:14.266
-You don't like being pranked?
-No.

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:15.601
-Do you like pranking people?
-No.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.503
-No? Okay.
I love pranking people.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:19.104
-Yeah.
-I'm obsessed.

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:20.740
I think I'm really good at it,

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.209
but I learned this season
that I'm not.

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:25.110
-Okay.
-I tried to prank everyone

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:27.446
on our show,
and I never pranked anyone.

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:29.582
They just pranked me.
-This is a really good --

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:31.884
I mean, I don't --
this is like less of a prank.

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:34.386
It's just a very impressive
piece of, like, crafting.

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.188
-This is insane.
This is insane.

00:07:36.188 --> 00:07:37.623
-Because this is what --
This is your car.

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:40.659
-They covered my car in like
3,000 Post-It notes on wrap day.

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:42.061
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:43.763
-And filled it
with stuffed animals.

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:45.297
That's --
Those are Post-It notes.

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.300
-Yeah.
-The entire crew was gone

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.435
one afternoon.
I didn't even notice.

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:51.570
And they were out covering
my car in this stuff.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:52.738
-Yeah.
-Can you believe that?

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:54.306
-This one is --
Can I just say this one --

00:07:54.306 --> 00:07:56.208
Is this -- this one's,
like, less impressive.

00:07:56.208 --> 00:07:58.110
I hope this happened before,
because after that one,

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.378
you'd be like --
-Oh, just "Stupid face"?

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:00.580
-Yeah, just "Stupid face."
-They put things on my --

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.648
"Stupid face."
-Yeah. I feel like you

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.216
wouldn't be like -- if somebody
came in and was like,

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:06.852
"I did this," and you were like,
"Oh, I did this."

00:08:06.852 --> 00:08:08.620
-"Stupid face!"
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:10.622
-They'd be like, "Wait.
Is it made out of Post-Its?"

00:08:10.622 --> 00:08:12.725
It's like, "No, I just wrote it
on one piece of paper."

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:14.826
-They always put a different
stupid name on my --

00:08:14.826 --> 00:08:17.262
on my chair, every single day
that I came in.

00:08:17.262 --> 00:08:19.699
-We have a video of you failing.
-Oh, my God.

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:21.200
In the dino outfit? Yes.
-Yeah.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.502
So explain what you wanted
to have happen.

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:26.672
-So, one of my co-stars told me
that he doesn't get scared.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:28.474
-Okay.
-Which is the t--

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:30.209
Now, of course,
I want to scare him, right?

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:31.777
I'm like, "Okay, now that
he told me this,

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:34.713
I got to figure something out."
So I ordered a dinosaur costume.

00:08:34.713 --> 00:08:36.515
-Okay.
-And I waited outside

00:08:36.515 --> 00:08:38.517
his trailer, which I thought
he was coming out.

00:08:38.517 --> 00:08:40.486
I ended up sitting in this thing
for like 20 minutes

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.922
waiting for him to come out.
And I had my team over there,

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:44.123
and they were giving me
the thumbs-up.

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:47.293
So he came out,
and I leaped at him.

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:50.095
This man is made of stone.
He didn't even flinch.

00:08:50.095 --> 00:08:51.964
-Yeah.
-I looked really scary.

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:53.031
-All right.

00:08:53.031 --> 00:08:54.733
-I thought I looked
really scary.

00:08:54.733 --> 00:08:56.268
-Okay.
I wish you hadn't said that,

00:08:56.268 --> 00:08:57.770
because we do have a clip
that will disprove

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:58.871
that theory immediately.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.871 --> 00:09:00.339
-Okay.
-Well, because I feel like

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:02.608
you're talking about --like,
everybody is picturing, like,

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:04.176
"Jurassic Park."
-T. Rex. Yeah.

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:05.578
-You're wearing
an inflatable dinosaur suit.

00:09:05.578 --> 00:09:07.780
-It was inf--
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.416
I thought it was terrifying
if this was jumping out at you.

00:09:10.416 --> 00:09:12.317
-All right, well, let's take a
look, and then we will judge

00:09:12.317 --> 00:09:14.720
whether or not you --
if you would have been terrified

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.557
if Kaley did this to you.
[ Laughs ]

00:09:18.557 --> 00:09:20.393
-[ Screaming ]

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:24.396
[ Laughter ]

00:09:24.396 --> 00:09:27.466
-He's just talking to me.
-It's really funny --

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:29.101
-Wouldn't that scare you?
-The best -- The best part

00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:31.970
is watching the kind of
disappointed dinosaur

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:33.506
talking to him.
-Like he's -- just with

00:09:33.506 --> 00:09:35.040
my hands like --
-Like, a dinosaur being like,

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:39.311
"Oh, I thought you'd be scared."
[ Laughter ]

00:09:39.311 --> 00:09:41.280
-How about that I stood
back there for 20 minutes?

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.048
-20 minutes?
-In that thing, sweating.

00:09:43.048 --> 00:09:44.583
-Yeah, I was going to say.
-I was shooting.

00:09:44.583 --> 00:09:46.518
I told them I was going
to the bathroom, and I went

00:09:46.518 --> 00:09:48.620
and got in that thing and waited
till he came out of his trailer.

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.689
-So you were -- the better prank
might have been on

00:09:50.689 --> 00:09:52.224
the rest of your crew that just
sat around waiting for you.

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:53.959
-For three extra hours?
Yeah. Yeah.

00:09:53.959 --> 00:09:55.828
That was the worst prank
that I did.

00:09:55.828 --> 00:09:58.597
Yes, they didn't laugh.
-Is it exciting,

00:09:58.597 --> 00:09:59.699
now that you finished
shooting it, to know

00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:00.899
that people are gonna
see it again?

00:10:00.899 --> 00:10:02.268
-Oh, my gosh.
-It's been a bit of a lay off,

00:10:02.268 --> 00:10:03.536
right?
-Yes. Yes.

00:10:03.536 --> 00:10:05.004
And, you know,
shooting through COVID

00:10:05.004 --> 00:10:06.838
and all these different things,
it's just so different now.

00:10:06.838 --> 00:10:08.273
And I just can't believe
we even finished it.

00:10:08.273 --> 00:10:09.542
But I'm thrilled
for people to see it.

00:10:09.542 --> 00:10:11.744
It is time to land this plane.
-Yeah.

00:10:11.744 --> 00:10:14.447
-But I'm super proud of it.
You know, it came from a book

00:10:14.447 --> 00:10:16.649
so many years ago, and I --
I don't know.

00:10:16.649 --> 00:10:18.384
I can't believe we're here
even talking about it.

00:10:18.384 --> 00:10:19.685
-Well, congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:10:19.685 --> 00:10:20.886
-It's really an amazing show.
-Thank you.

00:10:20.886 --> 00:10:22.321
-I'm so happy it's back
for a second season.

00:10:22.321 --> 00:10:23.689
I'm so happy to have you back
here with us in the studio.

00:10:23.689 --> 00:10:26.092
-Thank you, Seth.
-You guys, that's Kaley Cuoco!

00:10:26.092 --> 00:10:27.893
Second season
of "The Flight Attendant"

00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:29.428
returns to HBO Max tomorrow.

